  "page": 399,
  "line": 2,
  "situation": "The Confession of Faith opens by confessing unbelief. *I believe, Lord; help Thou mine unbelief* is the father of the epileptic boy's cry in Mark ix. 24, and it is set before the first article, as the door into the Creed. The Creed is not being recited but prayed, which is why every article below will be followed by what it is *for*.",
