 {
  "book": "mark",
  "chapter": 14,
  "verses": [
   33
  ],
  "printed": "Mark xiv. 33",
  "page": 310,
  "line": 7,
  "situation": "A wrong chapter, and it is the 1853 editor's, not Andrewes'. The square brackets are his mark for a reference he supplied, and `[*Mar.* xiii. 33.]` sends the reader to *take ye heed, watch and pray*. The words above it are *Tædere* and *Pavere*, and those two are the Vulgate of Mark xiv. 33 — *coepit pavere et tædere* — verbatim and in that order, so the verse is not in doubt and only the figure is. The following `[*Ibid.*]` inherits the error. Kept as printed, like every other, and named here because a reader who checks it will find nothing.",
  "source": "identified",
  "band": "R",
  "numbering": true,
  "plateFigure": true
 },
